+ # Upbit Trading Engine (Cron-safe)
+ This skill is designed to run **reliably from OpenClaw Cron** (Gateway scheduler) without relying on `OPENCLAW_TOOLS` being present in the child process.
+ **Core strategy (unchanged):**
+ - **Entry (buy):** Daily volatility breakout (`k=0.5`) AND 60-minute candle is bullish.
+ - **Exit (sell):** PnL-based take-profit / stop-loss (defaults: +5% / -5%).
+ ## What Cron should send (STRICT MODE)
+ To avoid model ambiguity and to make Cron runs deterministic, Cron messages **must be one of these exact forms**:
+ - `STRICT: monitor_once`
+ - `STRICT: worker_once`
+ - `STRICT: smoke_test`
+ If the message is not one of the above, do not trade. Reply with a short error and exit.
+ ## What the agent must do on each run
+ When invoked (especially by Cron):
+ 1) Read `{baseDir}/config.json` and validate required fields.
+ 2) Run exactly one of the following commands via the **exec tool** (workspace = `{baseDir}`):
+    - `node skill.js monitor_once`
+    - `node skill.js worker_once`
+    - `node skill.js smoke_test`
+ 3) Print the command that was executed and a short summary of results.
+ 4) Never require `OPENCLAW_TOOLS` in the Node process. Do not import OpenClaw SDKs.
+ ## Cron setup (recommended)
+ Use **isolated** jobs so each run is clean and does not accumulate chat history.
+ ### Monitor job (every 5 minutes)
+ ```bash
+ ```bash
+ ```bash
+ ```bash
+ openclaw cron add \
+ openclaw cron add \
+   --name "Upbit monitor (5m)" \
+   --cron "*/5 * * * *" \
+   --tz "Asia/Seoul" \
+   --tz "Asia/Seoul" \
+   --session isolated \
+   --session isolated \
+   --message "STRICT: monitor_once" \
+   --delivery none
+   --delivery none
+ ```
+ ```
+ ```
+ ```
+ ```
+ ### Worker job (every 1 minute)
+   --name "Upbit worker (1m)" \
+   --cron "* * * * *" \
+   --message "STRICT: worker_once" \
+ Notes:
+ - Cron runs an **agent turn** (`payload.kind = "agentTurn"`) in an isolated session.
+ - If you want notifications, switch to `--announce --channel <...> --to <...>` (see Cron docs).
+ ## Preventing NO_TOOLS (important)
+ If you see `code: "NO_TOOLS"`, it usually means the agent run has no tools enabled (often due to tool policy / allowlists).
+ Make sure the **exec tool is allowed** for the agent that Cron runs under:
+ - `exec` is the built-in tool used to run `node ...` commands.
+ - Tool availability is controlled by OpenClaw tool policy (`tools.allow` / `tools.deny`, per-agent tools config).
+ If you are using allowlists, ensure `exec` is included for the cron agent:
+ ```json5
+ {
+   tools: { allow: ["exec"] },
+   agents: {
+     list: [
+       { id: "main", tools: { allow: ["exec"] } }
+     ]
+   }
+ }
+ ## Local setup
+ 1) Copy `{baseDir}/config.example.json` to `{baseDir}/config.json` (do NOT commit `config.json`).
+ 2) Install deps:
+ npm ci
